Common QA tools for simplifying works
======================================

1. MongoDB Compass
--------------------
GUI tool for exploring and validating MongoDB data. Very beginner-level tool for Schema analysis, finding null values, checking field types etc.

2. DBeaver
----------
Free open-source database client. Supports MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, SQLite, SQL Server, etc. and useful for running SQL queries, data validation, exporting data, comparing datasets etc.

3. Jupyter Notebook
-------------------
Excellent for Data QA using Python, it can be used to create reusable validation scripts for null checks, duplicate checks, schema validation, generating QA reports etc.

4. OpenRefine
--------------
Extremely useful for cleaning and profiling CSV/Excel files. it features are cluster similar values, find inconsistent spellings, remove duplicates, transform columns etc. and it is great for non-programmers.


5. Great Expectations
----------------------
Highly recommended for Data QA. We can automatically validate null percentages, data types, value ranges, uniqueness, regex patterns etc.

6. Apache Superset
------------------
Useful for visually spotting data anomalies and trends.

7. KNIME Analytics Platform
---------------------------
It s a visual drag-and-drop data analytics and QA platform.


------------ OpenRefine -------------
=====================================

By creating a project and loading data into it , we can easily find Rows, Columns, Sort, Facets and Text filters .
a) Check null values - Column → Facet → Customized Facets → Facet by Blank
b) Count unique values - Column → Facet → Text Facet
c) Detect Invalid Categories - Use facets
d) Find duplicate values - Column → Facet → Text Facet
e) Filter rows - Column → Text Filter
f) Numeric QA - Column → Facet → Numeric Facet
g) Sort Data - Column → Sort
e) Regex valdation - Column → Text fiter → Enable regular expression → Give regex and enter


Advantages
----------
* No coding
* Easy profiling
* Powerful Faceting and Filtering
* Handle large dataset (500K–2M rows for 16 GB RAM)
*

Limitations
-----------
* Difficult to validate business rules
* Entire dataset is loaded locally
* Limited automation

